theory.intro:
An **arc** is part of the circumference of a circle. Its length $l$ is the radius $r$ multiplied by the central angle $\theta$, measured in radians. Convert any angle given in degrees before using the formula.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (3,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (-1.5,2.598);
\draw (O) circle (3);
\draw[thick] (O) -- (P) node[midway, below] {$r$};
\draw[thick] (O) -- (Q) node[midway, above left] {$r$};
\draw[thick, blue] (P) arc (0:120:3) node[midway, above right] {$l$};
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=0.8cm, angle eccentricity=1.6] {angle=P--O--Q};
\node[below left] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

